Subject: [PATCH] metal: compile a compute pipeline for the threadgroup size the guest dispatches

The driver picks a compute pipeline's maxTotalThreadsPerThreadgroup from the
kernel's register use, and it differs between GPUs. Measured on an iPhone
(A16): a guest kernel dispatched 1024-wide came back limited to 704, and the
dispatch was refused with metal_compute_threadgroup_limit_exceeded — work a
guest application was waiting on, never done.

When a dispatch needs more than the pipeline allows, the kernel is compiled
again with maxTotalThreadsPerThreadgroup set to the size the guest asked for,
which makes the compiler fit it (spilling registers if it must). The result
is kept in a cache of its own, since the main one matches on blob and stage
input only. If the driver still cannot, the dispatch is refused as before.
metal_compute_pso_sized reports each attempt.

diff --git a/crates/reims-vgpu/src/backend/metal/compute.rs b/crates/reims-vgpu/src/backend/metal/compute.rs
index fe4a71b8..96e369f7 100644
--- a/crates/reims-vgpu/src/backend/metal/compute.rs
+++ b/crates/reims-vgpu/src/backend/metal/compute.rs
@@ -62,6 +62,58 @@ fn new_compute_pipeline_state_uncached(
     }
 }
 
+/// A compute pipeline compiled to take `threads` per threadgroup.
+///
+/// Without a hint the driver picks the limit from the kernel's register use,
+/// and it differs between GPUs: measured on an iPhone (A16), a guest kernel a
+/// Mac runs 1024-wide came back limited to 704, and the dispatch was refused —
+/// work a guest application was waiting on, never done. Asking for the size the
+/// guest dispatches makes the compiler fit it, spilling registers if it must;
+/// the hardware takes up to 1024. `None` when the driver still cannot, and the
+/// caller refuses the dispatch as before.
+///
+/// Kept apart from the main cache, whose entries match on blob and stage input
+/// only: the same kernel compiled for two sizes is two pipelines.
+fn sized_compute_pipeline_state(
+    device: &Device,
+    function: &Function,
+    mtlb: &[u8],
+    stage_input: Option<&ReimsVgpuComputeStageInputDescriptor>,
+    threads: u64,
+) -> Option<ComputePipelineState> {
+    use parking_lot::Mutex;
+    static SIZED: Mutex<Vec<(u64, u64, u64, ComputePipelineState)>> = Mutex::new(Vec::new());
+    let blob = hash_bytes(mtlb);
+    let stage = hash_compute_stage_input(stage_input);
+    if let Some((.., pso)) = SIZED
+        .lock()
+        .iter()
+        .find(|(b, s, t, _)| *b == blob && *s == stage && *t == threads)
+    {
+        return Some(pso.clone());
+    }
+    let descriptor = ComputePipelineDescriptor::new();
+    descriptor.set_compute_function(Some(function));
+    if let Some(si) = stage_input {
+        let stage_descriptor =
+            make_compute_stage_input_descriptor(si, (ptr::null_mut(), 0)).ok()?;
+        descriptor.set_stage_input_descriptor(Some(&stage_descriptor));
+    }
+    descriptor.set_max_total_threads_per_threadgroup(threads);
+    let pso = device.new_compute_pipeline_state(&descriptor).ok()?;
+    let fits = pso.max_total_threads_per_threadgroup() >= threads;
+    crate::observe::fail(format!(
+        "metal_compute_pso_sized threads={threads} limit={} result={}",
+        pso.max_total_threads_per_threadgroup(),
+        if fits { "fits" } else { "still_short" }
+    ));
+    if !fits {
+        return None;
+    }
+    SIZED.lock().push((blob, stage, threads, pso.clone()));
+    Some(pso)
+}
+
